---
description: Iron rule — every closable screen/modal must support drag-down to dismiss
alwaysApply: true
---

# Drag-down to dismiss (กฎเหล็ก)

Any UI that can be closed (X / ปิด / back that dismisses a modal) **must** also close by dragging down.

## How to implement

### Expo Router screens (`presentation: 'modal' | 'fullScreenModal'`)

```ts
import { dismissibleModalOptions } from '@/shared/components/DragDownDismiss';

<Stack.Screen
  name="example"
  options={{
    presentation: 'modal', // or fullScreenModal
    ...dismissibleModalOptions,
  }}
/>
```

### React Native `<Modal>` / custom overlays

Wrap content with `DragDownDismiss`:

```tsx
import { DragDownDismiss } from '@/shared/components/DragDownDismiss';

<Modal visible={visible} transparent animationType="slide" onRequestClose={onClose}>
  <DragDownDismiss onDismiss={onClose} showDim rootInModal style={{ flex: 1 }}>
    {/* sheet content */}
  </DragDownDismiss>
</Modal>
```

If the sheet has a vertical `ScrollView` / `FlatList`, pass `scrollY` (Reanimated `SharedValue`) so dismiss only starts when scrolled to the top.

## Do not

- Ship a closable fullscreen/modal with only an X button and no drag-down.
- Disable `gestureEnabled` on dismissible modals unless there is an explicit product reason (document it).
